
# ── type(scope): subject ──────── keep the first line under 72 characters ──
#
# type:    feat | fix | physics | content | perf | refactor | docs | test
#          style | build | ci | chore | revert
# scope:   optional; the game or area, e.g. snooker, carrom, physics, lessons,
#          3d, ui, analytics, seo, deps
# subject: a command in lower case, no full stop: "add", "fix", "tune", not
#          "added" or "fixes". Add ! after the scope for a breaking change.
#
# Examples:
#   fix(physics): stop the cue ball sticking to the cushion at low speed
#   content(pool): add a stop-shot drill for the side pocket
#   feat(3d)!: replace the camera presets with free orbit
#
# Then a blank line, and a body saying what changed and why (wrap at ~72).
# Reference issues at the end: "Fixes #123" or "Refs #45".
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. See CONTRIBUTING.md#commit-messages.
